  "notes": "TCL QM6K Pro Google TV, 2025, US (device G08, model \"Smart TV Pro\", MediaTek tcl9618)\nAndroid 14 (Google TV), firmware UTT2.250416.001 AU16\nAlso seen on the same G08 board with AU14 firmware, a \"Smart TV Pro\" sold outside the US (prasta1, PR #23);\nthat set needed Wireless-debugging pairing (README, Troubleshooting).\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/tcl-qm6k-google-tv/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/tcl-qm6k-google-tv/debloat.txt com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nStock launcher: com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx. Live TV / HDMI app: com.tcl.tv.\nKeep: com.tcl.tv, com.tcl.tvinput, com.tcl.dashboard, com.tcl.suspension, com.tcl.autopair,\ncom.tcl.systemserver, com.tcl.providers.config, com.tcl.initsetup, com.tcl.useragreement,\ncom.tcl.globalkeyoverlay, com.tcl.systemui.plugin, com.tcl.factory.view and all com.mediatek.*.\nUnlike the 2023 G10 sets, com.tcl.ttvs and com.tcl.logkit ship ENABLED here.\nDo NOT disable com.tcl.providers.config, com.tcl.initsetup or com.tcl.factory.view: together they dropped\nthe Wi-Fi connection outright on the AU14 set and it took a re-pair over ADB to get back in (#23).\n\nKnown quirks on this firmware:\n- Play Protect blocks the launcher (\"built for an older version of Android\") unless targetSdk >= 34.\n- With launcherx disabled, setupwraith's RecoveryActivity claims HOME at priority 1 and shows a blank\nscreen. Shell can't disable that one component, so the whole package is disabled below (it only\nruns first-time setup). While Home was blank the TV fell back to HDMI 1 and woke a console over CEC.\n- Gear (keycode 83) and YouTube (190) only reach launcherx, so both go dead once it is disabled.\nconfig.json here maps them again; install the launcher with HOME_KEY_SERVICE=1 so the accessibility\nservice binds and reads them, then push the theme:\nTV_HOST=<tv ip> HOME_KEY_SERVICE=1 launcher/build-and-install.sh\nTV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/theme.sh examples/tcl-qm6k-google-tv\n- Soundbar on optical (S/PDIF) can't be powered or volume-controlled by the TV. Use HDMI 4 (eARC) and\n`cmd hdmi_control cec_setting set system_audio_control 1` (it ships 0 here).\nTCL tracking and analytics",
